================================================================================
CHALLENGE 3: THE SECURE TERMINAL (Switch & Do-While)
================================================================================
Context: Simulating a command-line interface with a retry limit.
1. Use a 'do-while' loop to keep a menu active.
2. Use a 'Scanner' to take user input (1-4).
3. Logic:
   - Use a 'switch' statement to handle choices.
   - Case 1: Print "Checking System...".
   - Case 2: Print "Updating Logs...".
   - Case 3: Print "Secure Exit Selected".
   - Default: Increment a 'wrongAttempts' counter.
4. The Twist:
   - If 'wrongAttempts' reaches 3, use 'break' to force-close the loop.
   - Print "System Locked: Too many invalid attempts" only if the loop
     closed due to errors.